  "content": [
    {
      "text": "Anything to eat; food; a meal (not necessarily flesh) (Gen. 1:29–30; Lev. 22:11, 13; 2 Sam. 13:5; Isa. 62:8; Ezek. 47:12; Hab. 3:17; Acts 16:34). In KJV meat is sometimes used to connote an offering made of grain (“meat offering”) but no flesh is involved, as in Ex. 29:41; 30:9; Lev. 2:1–15. See also Alma 8:21–22.",
